Scheduler Functions for Periodic Messaging and Status Retrieval\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/niuhuan/rust_proc_qq/main/docs/SchedulerJob.md\n\n```\n/// 每1分钟发送一次 Hello\n#[scheduler_job(cron = \"0 0/1 * * * ?\")]\nasync fn handle_scheduler(c:Arc<Client>) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n    let chain = MessageChain::default()\n        .append(Text::new(\"Hello\".to_owned()));\n    c.send_friend_message(123123,chain).await.expect(\"sent message failed\");\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n/// 每3分钟 获取一次网络状态\n#[scheduler_job(repeat = 180)]\nasync fn handle_scheduler02(c:Arc<Client>) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n    println!(\"{}\",c.get_status());\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n/// scheduler\npub fn scheduler() -> Scheduler {\n    scheduler!(\n        \"hello_jobs\",\n        handle_scheduler,\n        handle_scheduler02,\n    )\n}\n```\n\n## Cron Expression Format for Elasticsearch Scheduling\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/elastic/elasticsearch/main/docs/reference/elasticsearch/rest-apis/api-conventions.md\n\n```\n<seconds> <minutes> <hours> <day_of_month> <month> <day_of_week> [year]\n```\n\n## Defines Cron Expression Format for Apex Scheduled Jobs\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/labulakalia/ibm_bak/main/ibm_articles/Apex基础知识合辑.md\n\n```\n(Seconds,Minutes,Hours,Day_of_month,Month,Day_of_week,Optional_year)\n```\n\n## ari-m/convex-rules - Continue Hub\n\nhttps://hub.continue.dev/ari-m/convex-rules\n\n```\nexport default function App() { return Hello World; }\n```\n\n## tl Result 1\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/IppClub/Dora-SSR/main/Docs/docs/api/Class/Director.mdx\n\n```\nconst postScheduler: Scheduler\n```\n\n## Defines Scheduled Functions in AWS Arc with Cron Expressions\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/architect/arc.codes/main/src/views/docs/en/guides/backend/scheduled-functions.md\n\n```\n/\n├── src/\n│   └── scheduled/\n│       ├── daily-update-buddy/\n│       └── friday-only/\n├── app.arc\n└── package.json\n```\n\n## Setup Monthly Cron Job for Invoice Generation\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/get-convex/convex-backend/main/npm-packages/docs/docs/agents/usage-tracking.mdx\n\n```\nimport { cronJobs } from \"convex/server\";\nimport { internal } from \"./_generated/api\";\n\nconst crons = cronJobs();\n\n// Generate invoices for the previous month\ncrons.monthly(\n  \"generateInvoices\",\n  // Wait a day after the new month starts to generate invoices\n  { day: 2, hourUTC: 0, minuteUTC: 0 },\n  internal.usage.generateInvoices,\n  {},\n);\n\nexport default crons;\n```\n\n## Bosma::Scheduler Task Scheduling with Cron and Intervals\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/Bosma/Scheduler/main/README.md\n\n```\n#include \"Scheduler.h\"\n\n  // number of tasks that can run simultaneously\n  // Note: not the number of tasks that can be added,\n  //       but number of tasks that can be run in parallel\n  unsigned int max_n_threads = 12;\n\n  // Make a new scheduling object.\n  // Note: s cannot be moved or copied\n  Bosma::Scheduler s(max_n_threads);\n\n  // every second call message(\"every second\")\n  s.every(1s, message, \"every second\");\n\n  // in one minute\n  s.in(1min, []() { std::cout << \"in one minute\" << std::endl; });\n\n  // in one second run lambda, then wait a second, run lambda, and so on\n  // different from every in that multiple instances of the function will not be run concurrently\n  s.interval(1s, []() {\n    std::this_thread::sleep_for(5s);\n    std::cout << \"once every 6s\" << std::endl;\n  });\n\n  s.every(1min, []() { std::cout << \"every minute\" << std::endl; });\n\n  // https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cron\n  s.cron(\"* * * * *\", []() { std::cout << \"top of every minute\" << std::endl; });\n\n  // Time formats supported:\n  // %Y/%m/%d %H:%M:%S, %Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S, %H:%M:%S\n  // With only a time given, it will run tomorrow if that time has already passed.\n  // But with a date given, it will run immediately if that time has already passed.\n  s.at(\"2017-04-19 12:31:15\", []() { std::cout << \"at a specific time.\" << std::endl; });\n\n  s.cron(\"5 0 * * *\", []() { std::cout << \"every day 5 minutes after midnight\" << std::endl; });\n```\n\n## Defines Scheduled Functions with Rate and Cron Expressions\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/architect/arc.codes/main/src/views/docs/en/reference/project-manifest/scheduled.md\n\n```\n@app\nmyapp\n\n@scheduled\ndaily-update-buddy rate(1 day)\nfriyay-only cron(0 15 ? * FRI *)\n# verbose custom source:\nannual-review\n  rate 1 year\n  src custom/source\n```\n\n## Configure Intervals for Scheduled Function Execution\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/saml-dev/gome-assistant/main/README.md\n\n```\n// run every hour at the 30-minute mark\ninterval := ga.NewInterval().Call(myFunc).Every(\"1h\").StartingAt(\"00:30\").Build()\n// run every 5 minutes between 10am and 5pm\ninterval = ga.NewInterval().Call(myFunc).Every(\"5m\").StartingAt(\"10:00\").EndingAt(\"17:00\").Build()\n```\n\n## Scheduler Task Management with Custom Intervals and Cron\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/2881099/FreeScheduler/main/readme.md\n\n```\n//每5秒触发，执行N次\nvar id = scheduler.AddTask(\"topic1\", \"body1\", round: -1, 5);\n\n//每次 不同的间隔秒数触发，执行6次\nvar id = scheduler.AddTask(\"topic1\", \"body1\", new [] { 5, 5, 10, 10, 60, 60 });\n\n//每天 20:00:00 触发，执行N次（注意设置时区 UseTimeZone）\nvar id = scheduler.AddTaskRunOnDay(\"topic1\", \"body1\", round: -1, \"20:00:00\");\n\n//每周一 20:00:00 触发，执行1次\nvar id = scheduler.AddTaskRunOnWeek(\"topic1\", \"body1\", round: 1, \"1:20:00:00\");\n\n//每月1日 20:00:00 触发，执行12次\nvar id = scheduler.AddTaskRunOnMonth(\"topic1\", \"body1\", round: 12, \"1:20:00:00\");\n//每月最后一日 20:00:00 触发，执行12次\nvar id = scheduler.AddTaskRunOnMonth(\"topic1\", \"body1\", round: 12, \"-1:20:00:00\");\n\n//自定义间隔 cron\nvar id = scheduler.AddTaskCustom(\"topic1\", \"body1\", \"0/1 * * * * ? \");\nnew FreeSchedulerBuilder()\n    ...\n    .UseCustomInterval(task =>\n    {\n        //利用 cron 功能库解析 task.IntervalArgument 得到下一次执行时间\n        //与当前时间相减，得到 TimeSpan，若返回 null 则任务完成\n        return TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5);\n    })\n    .Build();\n```\n\n## Schedule and Clear Cron Jobs with schedule and clearSchedule\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/main/src-editor/src/OpenAi/docs.md\n\n```\nlet sch = schedule('*/2 * * * *', () => {\n    /* ... */\n});\n\n// later:\nclearSchedule(sch);\n```\n\n## ScheduleService Class with Cron Job and Locking Mechanism\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/miaowing/nest-schedule/main/README.md\n\n```\nimport { Injectable } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { Cron, NestDistributedSchedule } from 'nest-schedule';\n\n@Injectable()\nexport class ScheduleService extends NestDistributedSchedule {  \n  constructor() {\n    super();\n  }\n  \n  async tryLock(method: string) {\n    if (lockFail) {\n      return false;\n    }\n    \n    return () => {\n      // Release here.\n    }\n  }\n  \n  @Cron('0 0 4 * *')\n  async cronJob() {\n    console.log('executing cron job');\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Create Schedule with Schedules SDK using Cron Format\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/triggerdotdev/trigger.dev/main/docs/tasks/scheduled.mdx\n\n```\nconst createdSchedule = await schedules.create({\n  //The id of the scheduled task you want to attach to.\n  task: firstScheduledTask.id,\n  //The schedule in cron format.\n  cron: \"0 0 * * *\",\n  //this is required, it prevents you from creating duplicate schedules. It will update the schedule if it already exists.\n  deduplicationKey: \"my-deduplication-key\",\n});\n```\n\n## Schedule and Clear Cron Jobs in JavaScript\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.javascript/main/docs/en/javascript.md\n\n```\nlet sch = schedule('*/2 * * * *', () => { /* ... */ });\n\n// later:\nclearSchedule(sch);\n```\n\n## Cron Job Triggering Every 90 Seconds on Weekdays\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/Hexagon/croner/main/docs/src/usage/examples.md\n\n```\n// Trigger on specific interval combined with cron expression\nnew Cron('* * 7-16 * * MON-FRI', { interval: 90 }, function () {\n\tconsole.log('This will trigger every 90th second at 7-16 on mondays to fridays.');\n});\n```\n\n## Schedule Resource with Cron and Rate Triggering Functions\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/winglang/wing/main/docs/contributing/999-rfcs/2023-01-20-wingsdk-spec.md\n\n```\nresource Schedule {\n  /**\n   * Trigger events according to a cron schedule.\n   * @example \"0 0 * * *\" - midnight every day\n   */\n  static fromCron(cron: str): Schedule;\n\n  /**\n   * Trigger events at a periodic rate.\n   * @example 1 hour\n   */\n  static fromRate(rate: duration): Schedule;\n\n  private init(/* elided */): Schedule;\n\n  /**\n   * Run an inflight whenever the schedule triggers.\n   */\n  onTick(fn: inflight () => void, opts: ScheduleOnTickProps?): void;\n}\n\nstruct ScheduleOnTickProps { /* elided */ }\n```\n\n## ScheduledTaskConfig Interface for Task Scheduling in Vendure\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/vendure-ecommerce/vendure/main/docs/docs/reference/typescript-api/scheduled-tasks/scheduled-task.md\n\n```\ninterface ScheduledTaskConfig<C extends Record<string, any> = Record<string, any>> {\n    id: string;\n    description?: string;\n    params?: C;\n    schedule: string | ((cronTime: typeof CronTime) => string);\n    timeout?: number | string;\n    preventOverlap?: boolean;\n    execute(args: ScheduledTaskExecutionArgs<C>): Promise<any>;\n}\n```\n\n## Defines scheduled function for Cloudflare Worker cron jobs\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/ruanyf/articles/main/dev/cloudflare-worker/cron.md\n\n```\nexport default {\n  async scheduled(event, env, ctx) {\n    // ...\n  },\n};\n```\n\n## Defines Scheduled Function with @tomodachi.schedule Decorator\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/kalaspuff/tomodachi/main/README.md\n\n```\n@tomodachi.schedule(\n    interval=None,\n    timestamp=None,\n    timezone=None,\n    immediately=False,\n)\ndef handler(self, *args, **kwargs):\n    ...\n```\n\n## Cronvex\n\nhttps://convex.de